.TH PINBALL 1
.SH NAME
pinball \- Orbit 9 space pinball
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B games/pinball
[
.B -ad
] [
.B -n
.I frames
] [
.B -o
.I image.png
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Pinball
plays a three-ball game on an original space-themed table.
It runs in a rio window using raylib and VirGL.
.PP
Hold Space to compress the launch spring, then release it.
Z or the left arrow operates the left flipper;
slash or the right arrow operates the right flipper.
The up arrow nudges the table. Three rapid nudges tilt it,
disabling flippers, scoring, bonus and ball saving until the next ball.
P pauses, R starts a new game and Q quits.
Losing keyboard focus pauses an active game; P resumes it.
.PP
Hit the three left-hand relay targets, then five reactor bumpers,
then shoot upward into the right-hand orbit ramp to complete a mission.
Missions carry across balls. The ramp returns the ball to the left inlane.
Lighting all three upper rollovers increases the multiplier;
the rollovers reset after each completed mission or new ball.
.PP
Bumpers award 100 points, slingshots 50, relay targets 250,
rollovers 500, the ramp 2000 and a completed mission 25000,
each multiplied by the current multiplier (at most five).
An additional bonus is collected when the ball drains unless tilted.
The first eight seconds of play on each ball have a ball saver.
A saved ball is served again without renewing the timer.
The best score lasts for the current process.
.PP
.B -a
enables synthesized effects through
.BR /dev/audio .
.B -d
plays an automatic demonstration; R takes over with a new game.
.B -n
exits after the specified number of frames, advancing the simulation by
exactly 1/60 second per unpaused frame.
.B -o
saves the final window image as PNG.
The window may be resized; the table retains its proportions.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/games/pinball
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR raylib (2),
.IR gpu (3),
.IR rio (4)
